# Line-ending conversion is for text, and a PDF is not text.
#
# The synthetic PDFs in demo-documents/ are written by tests/pdfbuild*.py with
# uncompressed, all-ASCII streams, so git's content sniffing classifies them as text.
# Under Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true a checkout then rewrote every LF
# inside them as CRLF: each file grew by tens of bytes, every xref offset and stream
# /Length went stale, strict PDF readers refused them, and the same commit hashed
# differently on a Windows clone and a Linux one. `binary` (-text -diff -merge) stores
# and checks out the exact bytes the generator wrote, on every platform.
# tests/test_licensing_and_branding.py holds this in place.
*.pdf binary
